{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuditOutcome"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AuditOutcome","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carrying an unrecognised value back into an update is refused by the server rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written as a spelling it never used. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}],"type":"p